  "term": "electrooculography",
  "definition": "Electrooculography is a biological recording of the resting electrical potential between the cornea and retina while the eyes move a set distance right and left under dark and light adaptation. The change in this potential with light adaptation is used to assess the retinal pigment epithelium.",
